    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s original name was Unionville, named after the 1797 Union Church, before becoming Neffs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neffs%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1884 a Coach Factory began producing sleighs, wagons, and carriages, marking Neffs’ first industrial venture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/neffs_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first non‑agricultural plant opened in 1967 when Ted Ambrosino founded Ambro Fashions, the town’s first factory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
